
remstart
    THE LIST OF WHAT IS ON THE BOARD (a prototype, 2026-10-24)
    in info mode, the outline on the whole board says that the confirm key lists everything that is on
    it. the list comes up on the left: one row for each kind of thing that is out there, with how many
    there are, like "Jellyfish 3", "Upside Down Fish 2", "Facing Left 31". the kinds are the ones of
    THE THINGS ON THE BOARD, IN INFO MODE, in fish_headers_boardinfo, with the way that the fish face
    split in two.

    the row that is chosen is the spotlight: the dark of info mode opens up over every cell that has that
    kind of thing on it, and only those, with a hole of its own on each cell. holes that touch run
    together, so a patch of coral shows as one block. the holes grow in, a little past their size and
    back, every time the row changes. and copies of a few of those fish fly out of their cells, over to
    the number in the row, and pop there. the fish themselves never leave their cells, so the player can
    still see where everything is.

    {dir} goes up and down the list. the confirm key goes back to the board, and the info key leaves
    info mode, the same as always. the mouse chooses a row by going over it, and a click anywhere else
    goes back to the board.
    ASKING THE ANGLER (2026-10-27). with a light kept, the confirm key on a row, or a click on it, spends
    the light, and the angler's first question is about that row: every kind has a topic of its own (see
    anglerKindTopic, in fish_routines_angler). the hint says so. without a light it goes back, as above.

    LOOKING CLOSER (2026-10-27). Chris: the confirm key on the whole board no longer opens the list. it puts
    a cursor of info mode's own on a cell, the one that the game's cursor is on, and the same panel on the
    left has a row for every thing about that cell, each with its words under it: what is in it (a fish,
    a jellyfish, the squid...), what is the matter with the fish (rainbow, belly up, stacked, ringed, the
    way that it faces), and what is under it (coral, horror coral, ink). a cell with nothing to say about
    it has a row for the plain fish. the number on a row is how many of that there are on the whole board.
    {dir} moves the cursor from cell to cell, and the rows follow it. off the edge of the board, it goes
    back to the rest of info mode, in that direction.
    the confirm key on a cell chooses its rows: {dir} up and down goes from row to row, and the chosen row
    is the spotlight of the list, on every cell of the board that has it, with the copies flying to its
    number. the confirm key on a row asks the angler about it, with a light kept, and otherwise goes back
    to moving the cursor. so does {dir} left and right, which moves the cursor on as well.
    the mouse: going over a cell looks at it, a click on a cell chooses its rows, a click on a row asks,
    and a click anywhere else goes back.
    the list itself is still here (spotOpen), and the look is built out of it (spotLookOpen): SPOT_LOOK is
    1 while it is the look. nothing opens the list any more.

    the routines are in fish_routines_spot. info mode comes to them with gosubs, because it is in a file
    that comes before the board is declared.
remend
global SPOT_ON = 0 `1 while the list is open
global SPOT_READY = 0 `1 once the sprites have been made
global SPOT_ROW_MAX = 20
global dim SPOT_ROW_KIND(20) `what each row is: one of the BOARD_INFO_ kinds, or SPOT_KIND_RIGHT
global dim SPOT_ROW_COUNT(20) `how many of it there are
global SPOT_ROWS = 0
global SPOT_SEL = 0 `the row that is chosen
global SPOT_KIND_RIGHT = 17 `the fish that face right. BOARD_INFO_FACING is the ones that face left, here.
global SPOT_KIND_SQUID = 18 `the squid. only the look has these three.
global SPOT_KIND_INK = 19 `a cell that is inked
global SPOT_KIND_FISH = 20 `a fish with nothing to say about it. it is only ever on the cell that is looked at.
global SPOT_KIND_CLEAN = 21 `a cell that the ink of the day has been washed off of. see CLEAN in fish_headers_squid.

` LOOKING CLOSER
global SPOT_LOOK = 0 `1 while the panel is the look at one cell, and not the list
global SPOT_LOCKED = 0 `1 while the rows of the cell are being chosen from, and the cursor stays put
global SPOT_LOOK_CELL = 0 `the cell that is looked at
global SPOT_LOOK_FROM_MOUSE = 0 `1 when a click opened the look, so that it starts on the cell under the mouse
global SPOT_LOOK_CURSOR as infoBorder `the outline on the cell
global dim SPOT_ROW_DESCS(20) `the words of every row, under it
global dim SPOT_ROW_Y(20) `where every row is, up and down, and how tall, with its words
global dim SPOT_ROW_HS(20)
global SPOT_LOOK_ALL_WORDS = 1 `0 when the words of every row would not fit, and only the chosen row has them

global dim SPOT_MATCH(400) `the cells that the chosen row is about
global SPOT_MATCH_N = 0
global dim SPOT_HOLES(400) `a hole in the dark for each of them
global SPOT_HOLES_MADE = 0
global SPOT_GROW_FROM = 0 `when the holes of the chosen row started to grow in
global SPOT_GROW_MS = 280
global SPOT_GROWN = 0 `1 once they have, so that they are left alone

` the copies that fly to the number. each one has a cell to come from, a row to go to, and a time to set off.
global SPOT_GHOST_MAX = 14
global dim SPOT_GHOSTS(14)
global dim SPOT_GHOST_CELL(14) `-1 for one that is not flying
global dim SPOT_GHOST_AT(14) `the game ms() that it sets off
global SPOT_GHOST_MS = 420 `how long it takes to get there
global SPOT_GHOST_STAGGER = 35 `how much later each one sets off than the one before

` the panel on the left
global SPOT_PANEL_SPRITE = 0
global SPOT_PANEL_BORDER as infoBorder
global SPOT_ROW_BAR_SPRITE = 0 `the light behind the row that is chosen
global SPOT_TITLE_TEXT_ID = 0
global SPOT_DESC_TEXT_ID = 0
global dim SPOT_ROW_TEXTS(20)
global dim SPOT_COUNT_TEXTS(20)
global SPOT_PANEL_X = 6
global SPOT_PANEL_Y = 0
global SPOT_PANEL_W = 150
global SPOT_PANEL_H = 0
global SPOT_ROW_H = 17
global SPOT_ROWS_TOP = 0 `where the first row is

remstart
    NEW INFO ON THE BOARD (2026-10-24). when an entry of the codec is new, and the thing that it is about is
    out on the board, the "new info!" badge of info mode goes there, instead of to the Codec spot: it dances
    over the one of them that is nearest the cursor, and turns into the little dot on the corner of its cell.
    every other new thing on the board just has the dot. the list has the dot too, on its row, and choosing
    the row reads it. the Codec spot keeps a dot of its own for what is new and is not on the board.
    the badge itself is drawn by codecNewStep, in fish_routines_teach. SPOT_NEW_ANCHOR says where.
remend
global dim SPOT_NEW_CELL(18) `for every kind, the cell of the one nearest the cursor while its entry is new, or -1
global SPOT_NEW_ANCHOR = -1 `the kind that the badge goes to, or -1 for the Codec spot
global SPOT_NEW_OFF_BOARD = 0 `how many new entries are not on the board
global dim SPOT_NEW_DOTS(19) `a dot for every kind, and the last one is for the Codec spot
global dim SPOT_ROW_DOTS(20)
global SPOT_NEW_READY = 0
global SPOT_READ_KIND = -1 `the kind of the row that is chosen, which is read when the list moves off it or closes
